# Model config

`lib/modelConfig.ts` is the **single source of truth** for image/video models.

## Add a model

1. Add an entry to `IMAGE_MODELS` or `VIDEO_MODELS` with `id`, `apiId`, `name`, `provider`, ratios/caps, and `apiInput` mapping.
2. Stop. UI dropdowns and generate routes derive from this file — do not hardcode model lists in nodes or API routes.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — hardcode in GenerateNode
const MODELS = [{ id: "foo", name: "Foo" }];

// ✅ GOOD — already done in GenerateNode
const MODELS = IMAGE_MODELS.map((m) => ({ id: m.id, name: m.name, meta: m.provider }));
```

## Providers

- Default backend: **kie.ai**. Per-model overrides: `lib/providers.ts` (`kie` | `azure` | `codex`).
- Azure / Codex are image-only; use `azureSizeMap` / related fields on the model entry when Azure applies.
- Task IDs: kie = opaque; Azure/Codex = prefixed `azure-…` / `codex-…`. Never poll kie for those (`lib/kieJobPoller.ts`).

## API payload mapping

- Build kie input from `apiInput` keys (`aspectRatioKey`, `imageInputKey`, `qualityKey`, `extra`, …).
- Honour `textOnlyApiId` when there are no reference images.
- Respect `promptMaxLength` / `textOnlyPromptMaxLength` and `maxImages`.

## Assistant LLM models

Text assistant models live in `lib/models.ts` (`MODEL_GROUPS`) — separate from image/video `modelConfig`.
